{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process, Rental Items are Returned to the Store."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause implicitly initiates the process and describes the first action of returning items."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3",
        "guard:b1->n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the items to the store,\" then we can continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the XOR decision structure, the resulting action, and the boolean guard representing the condition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4",
        "guard:b1->n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site,\" then we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly models the alternative delivery path and its corresponding branch guard."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the exclusive choice point and the action taken when the order is fully complete."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6",
        "guard:b2->n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Order is incomplete and items are missing,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Accurately captures the incomplete-order branch target and its condition guard."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7",
        "guard:b2->n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Similarly, if the \"Order is complete but items are damaged,\" we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the damage-condition split and the corresponding notification action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After this, if the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Action content faithfully restates the packing step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Alternatively, if the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to the storage-for-future-orders action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In case of missing items and replacement charges, we email the customer to inform them."
      ],
      "justification": "Preserves the core instruction to email the customer regarding replacement charges."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Additionally, if there are damaged items and additional charges, we temporarily take them out of inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "Accurately reflects the inventory removal step for damaged items."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15",
        "guard:b3->n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the missing items,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Maps the customer-return-missing-items action and its conditional guard."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n16",
        "guard:b3->n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the \"Customer does not return the missing items,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Correctly models the failure-to-return branch and its guard."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "The explicit termination step and structural end node align with the closing clause."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are repaired and added into inventory,\" we continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Action content matches the repair-and-restock instruction."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n12",
        "action:n13",
        "guard:b6->n12",
        "guard:b6->n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if the \"Items can't be repaired and are discarded,\" we email the customer with replacement charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the disposal decision split, the discard action, the subsequent email action, and both path guards."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n18"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Lastly, the items are packed for an existing order."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the final packing instruction; the surrounding conditional phrasing in the source is absorbed into the action node per standard modeling practice."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n19"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct correspondence to the storage action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n20"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once again, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Redundant terminal actions and end nodes collectively cover the repeated completion statement."
    }
  ],
